; Switchyard (issue #373, a large Hot Potato stage for five to eight players):
; two yards either side of a 500 px gap. Each yard is a floor with a raised
; platform above its inner end and a bounce pad on the edge that throws you onto
; it. Across the gap a shuttle carries players over the void, a spinning slab
; hangs below the raised bridge, and the bridge links the two yards across the
; top. Every route is a ring: floor -> pad -> platform -> bridge -> platform ->
; pad -> floor, or floor -> shuttle -> floor. Chasers cut the corner on the
; shuttle; the chased go over the top.
; 
; Large: the view is 2240 x 1260 (Stage.view_size). Terrain spans x = -1100..1100.
; Rotation (Stage.mode_weights): weighted 4x for Hot Potato, and in any other
; mode dealt into a bag only 30% of the time ("_other").
[node name="Switchyard" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("script")
background_sky_top = Color(0.1, 0.12, 0.14, 1)
background_sky_bottom = Color(0.2, 0.26, 0.26, 1)
background_silhouette = Color(0.08, 0.1, 0.1, 1)
background_layers = PackedStringArray("clouds", "city", "city")
view_size = Vector2(2240, 1260)
mode_weights = {"hot_potato": 4.0, "_other": 0.3}

; The two yards. Spawns sit on their outer ends.
